Titre$Resupinatus New Zealand Cooper2012
com$adapt GF 05/2017

1,0$ source :Mycological Notes 7 : Resupinatus species in New Zealand
1,0$ Intro : Resupinatus is a genus of small pleurotoid or cupulate dark coloured fungi on wood.///Stevenson had a fairly broad concept of Resupinatus and described species now shifted to Panellus, Campanellus, Pleurotus, Conchomyces and Marasmiellus. On the basis of better information of the boundaries of the genus at least some of those species should once again be considered as true Resupinatus and a few more species have been assigned to the genus or more recently recorded from New Zealand


1,3 $ Posessing laterally attached flabellate caps, with gills or merulioid or poroid hymenium.
1,2 $ fruiting bodies consisting of densely clustered cups
2,3 $ cups seated on a dense stroma
2,0 $ cups not seated on a dense stroma $ R. urceolatus
3,0 $ spores sublobose 5.5-7 x 5.5-6 µm $ R. poriaeformis
3,0 $ spores ellipsoid, 7-9 x 5-6.5 µm $ R. huia
4,6 $ cap microscopically covered with thick-walled hyphae ornamented with pegs, spores cylindrical or ellipsoidal
4,5 $ cap microscopically at most with small diverticulae, spores subglobose
5,0 $ Hymenium merulioid, cap without basal tomentum $ R. merulioides
5,0 $ Hyemenium normally gilled, cap with shaggy tomentum over basal area $ R. subapplicatus
6,0 $ regular gills, spores cylindrical $ R. violaceogriseus
6,0 $ gills cross-veined to poroid, spores ellipsoid $ R. vinosolividus

 µm 